      "text": "2 and NaCl enhanced adsorption of PFOS and PFOA to a CAC, but the effect on short-chain PFAA was not evaluated. DOM is also known to impact the adsorption of organic compounds onto AC [31] . DOM can decrease adsorption by physically blocking access to AC micropores and lead to electrostatic repulsion, with this being most predominant for shorter-chain PFAA [2,11,26] . DOM has also been shown to enhance adsorption of longer-chain PFAA through hydrophobic interaction with the perfluorinated alkyl tail [32] . In addition to DOM, the effect of anionic polymers used in the CAC delivery formulation, such as CMC, must also be evaluated as they may impact adsorption similarly to DOM [25] . For PlumeStop \u00ae , the proprietary delivery polymer had a negative impact on the adsorption of a range of PFAS [26] , but other CAC and polymer materials used in the field should be explored as both AC surface chemistry and PFAA structure alter the importance of either the electrostatic or hydrophobic thermodynamic driving force. There are key knowledge gaps regarding the use of CAC barriers for in situ remediation of PFAS. First, there has not been a systematic evaluation of how changes in water chemistry will impact the adsorp - tion behavior of short-chain PFAA, which will likely present the greatest challenge for barrier design."
